11583 {\cf20 // Note that a local position will vary depending on initial scroll value,}\par
11584 {\cf20 // This is a little bit confusing so bear with us:}\par
11585 {\cf20 //  - local_pos = (absolution_pos - window->Pos)}\par
11586 {\cf20 //  - So local_x/local_y are 0.0f for a position at the upper-left corner of a window,}\par
11587 {\cf20 //    and generally local_x/local_y are >(padding+decoration) && <(size-padding-decoration) when in the visible area.}\par
11588 {\cf20 //  - They mostly exist because of legacy API.}\par
11589 {\cf20 // Following the rules above, when trying to work with scrolling code, consider that:}\par
11590 {\cf20 //  - SetScrollFromPosY(0.0f) == SetScrollY(0.0f + scroll.y) == has no effect!}\par
11591 {\cf20 //  - SetScrollFromPosY(-scroll.y) == SetScrollY(-scroll.y + scroll.y) == SetScrollY(0.0f) == reset scroll. Of course writing SetScrollY(0.0f) directly then makes more sense}\par
11592 {\cf20 // We store a target position so centering and clamping can occur on the next frame when we are guaranteed to have a known window size}\par
