16134 {\cf20 // Docking: ImGuiDockContext}\par
16135 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
16136 {\cf20 // The lifetime model is different from the one of regular windows: we always create a ImGuiDockNode for each ImGuiDockNodeSettings,}\par
16137 {\cf20 // or we always hold the entire docking node tree. Nodes are frequently hidden, e.g. if the window(s) or child nodes they host are not active.}\par
16138 {\cf20 // At boot time only, we run a simple GC to remove nodes that have no references.}\par
16139 {\cf20 // Because dock node settings (which are small, contiguous structures) are always mirrored by their corresponding dock nodes (more complete structures),}\par
16140 {\cf20 // we can also very easily recreate the nodes from scratch given the settings data (this is what DockContextRebuild() does).}\par
16141 {\cf20 // This is convenient as docking reconfiguration can be implemented by mostly poking at the simpler settings data.}\par
16142 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
16143 {\cf20 // - DockContextInitialize()}\par
16144 {\cf20 // - DockContextShutdown()}\par
16145 {\cf20 // - DockContextClearNodes()}\par
16146 {\cf20 // - DockContextRebuildNodes()}\par
